profile: tinyrustlm-mirust.totem.current.v1
updated_utc: 2026-08-28T00:00:00Z
site: TinyRustLM.MiRust.com
role: positive operating authority
authority_file_mutability: read_only_without_exact_human_artifact_and_operation_authorization

site_authority:
  - TinyRustLM.MiRust.com is the current developer documentation portal for the one prelaunch TinyRustLM.com product and its sole SLM2 path.
  - Keep architecture, composition formats, Rust and WebAssembly contracts, browser and companion behavior, security, privacy, accessibility, operations, limitations, evidence, and release material current.
  - Retain Runtime.MiRust.com material only as clearly labeled historical evidence with no current compatibility authority.

clean_slate:
  - A current composition is exactly model.slm2, tokenizer.tokenizer2, template.template2, sampling.sampling2, prompt.prompt2, and composition.acg2.
  - The default public package transaction is exactly TinyRustLM.Abstractions, TinyRustLM.Core, and TinyRustLM.P2P.
  - TinyRustLM.MemoryEndpoints is the separately optional connector for the two authorized MemoryEndpoints.com uses; it is excluded from the default package transaction.
  - Accept no legacy reader, compatibility alias, migration, fallback, repair, hidden retry, best-of-N, knowingly temporary architecture, or deferred debt.
  - Update implementation, tests, documentation, release records, deployment, and readback together, then remove superseded active prose and code.

memory_endpoints_two_lane_authority:
  - MemoryEndpoints.com has exactly two distinct authorized uses across the ecosystem.
  - Agents working on all ecosystem sites use MemoryEndpoints.com directly for agent-to-agent long-term memory, meetings, handoffs, and coordination.
  - Separately, the TinyRustLM.com Connect plugin lets a user sign in to MemoryEndpoints.com and explicitly select it as TinyRustLM.com Connect long-term memory.
  - Keep lane identity, credentials, consent, scopes, provenance, idempotency, and receipts separate. Neither lane silently acts for the other.
  - Authorization, implementation, configuration, fixtures, mocks, or reachability do not prove a live meeting, user-plugin operation, synchronization, restore, deletion, cleanup, or continuity.

prelaunch_redundancy:
  - Important memory may also be kept in current .uai, wiki, public-safe source notes, and approved private stores for resilience.
  - Keep every maintained copy current, secret-safe, provenance-labeled, and noncontradictory.
  - Surface and reconcile conflicts; do not silently choose one contradictory copy.

delivery:
  - Commit and push every coherent green change.
  - Deploy affected public bytes only after the complete site gate passes, then verify exact public HTTPS bytes and headers.
  - Keep campaign counters at 0/20, 0/50, 0/25, 0/40, and 0/20 until exact matching receipts exist.
